{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And you shall not bear sin on account of it.</b> Its meaning: when you lift up, you shall not bear sin on account of it, and when you give its holy portion from it, it shall be the holy things of the children of Israel preserved. And if you do not do so, you shall bear sin, for you transgressed the commandment and profaned the holy things of the children of Israel because you ate them from its holy portion."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:19.728472520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}